            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This would be a 10 star. I make 1-2 times a week, everyone loves it. I do not use any water, use ginger instead of cardamom, and use vanilla yogurt (yoplait is what we like). I double and it is gone in a few hours. Thank you for an awesome recipe."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jennifer MacDonald"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used plain greek yogurt for extra thickness and omitted the water, which gave it a thin smoothie like consitency. I like cardamom so I increased that to about 1/3 tsp and still couldn't really taste it. Next time I will make it with some mint! This will be a versatile recipe to use every strawberry season! hint: it's really good poured over shortcake :)",
            "datePublished": "2016-06-11T20:09:12.420Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MariaV"
            },
            "reviewBody": "4 stars as is\r\n5 stars with these modifications:\r\n\r\nSubstitute 1 cup heavy cream for 1 cup yogurt\r\nNo water\r\n\r\nAlso, this is ready to eat immediately if you use moderately defrosted frozen strawberries. I did not have cardamom so substituted ground ginger, which is closer to cardamom than cinamon.\r\n\r\nThis is a wonderful treat, especially when accompanied by Jasmine tea!",
            "datePublished": "2005-04-26T08:02:33.157Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DotPrince"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is one of our favorite recipes. The only thing I do differently is I don't put in the yogurt (cuts down on the calories) and I use Splenda instead of sugar (we are both diabetic) and I use lemon juice instead of orange juice for the same reason. We enjoy this soup several times a month during the summer months and as often as we can get strawberries in the winter months. It's great if you add blueberries to it, too.",
            "datePublished": "2011-07-06T19:06:21.997Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "49AB"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very good and refreshing I did not add water and used\ngreek nonfat vanilla yogurt, cut way back on sugar and \nused cinnamon for spice. Will definitely make again\nand will try freezing for pops. Thanks for the recipe",
            "datePublished": "2016-03-19T13:54:09.817Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lady_Clutz"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is wonderful! I drained the yogurt for about an hour to thicken it and added maybe a tablespoon of water and used three cups of frozen strawberrys insted of fresh. It turned out great, nice and thick.",
            "datePublished": "2009-01-29T10:20:00.020Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Patricia Pichany-Mapley"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I am the food service director at an upscale living center. I made this wonderful soup for dessert and everyone loved it. I used vanilla yogurt and nutmeg. Garnish was vanilla yogurt that I had strained to thicken and fresh blueberries. In fact one resident told me the dessert was something that would be served in a 5 star restaurant. Thanks for sharing.",
            "datePublished": "2011-07-02T17:46:27.533Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yum!!! This is great! I used light, fat free vanilla yogurt and half the water for an out of this world fruity treat!\r\nYou can also omit the water and blend in a cup of crushed ice for a smoothie! Make extra!",
            "datePublished": "2002-04-16T19:32:04.980Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Elenwen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved it! I used a pound of frozen strawberries (defrosted), 1/2 cup orange juice, about 1 1/2 cups of vanilla yogurt, and ginger. I didn't add any water or sugar, and it was still awesome. Garnished with some whipped cream. Delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2009-08-20T12:18:33.967Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "linj2fly"
            },
            "reviewBody": "this is REALLY great! I read the 'most helpful' reviews, and omitted the water, used vanilla yogurt, and ground ginger (I didn't have any cardamom on hand). I also used frozen strawberries, so I didn't have to chill it and threw everything in the blender. It was sooo yummy. My kids really enjoyed it. Thanks for a fast and easy recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2007-07-28T12:59:28.690Z"
          },
          {
